      <h1 class="tg-hero__title">A Walk Through Church History</h1>
      <p class="tg-hero__intro">
        Two thousand years separate us from the upper room, and most of what fills that
        span is told to us secondhand — summarized, simplified, and bent to whoever is
        doing the summarizing. This study walks the whole road on the original pavement:
        every era described from its own documents — letters, liturgies, trial records,
        creeds, confessions — so you can see for yourself what the church looked like,
        what it believed, what it argued about, and what it fought against. And running
        through every era, one thread: the visible church that the world can see, and the
        invisible church that only the Lord can number.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="tg-hero__key-verse">
        <p>Nevertheless, God's firm foundation stands, bearing this inscription:
           "The Lord knows those who are His."</p>
        <cite><a class="ref" data-ref="2 Timothy 2:19">2 Timothy 2:19</a></cite>
      </blockquote>
